This was my attempt to build a compiler i had read about that will give around a 15% boost to your projects and tunes things up to your set-up.
I started out with the basic building blocks of oneAPI, oneTBB and oneDNN, they are I have found the building blocks of anything you want to do.
oneTBB is your schedule of how tasks and data are handled and its job is to just make those loads balance out just like you would do in a lot of different situations.
oneDNN is basically doing the brain work of optimizing the tasks and learning as it goes to make everything run faster and smoother like tuning a engine.
LLVM the compiler for oneAPI can be used to compile both oneTBB and oneDNN to better tune them to your setup.
Then after they are tuned it can be optimized by taking what you have done and rerunning the process with the tuned oneTBB and oneDNN over again.
